        for(int i=0;i<arr.length-1;i++){ 
 // if current element is greater than next,
            // array is not sorted in increasing order
            if(arr[i]>arr[i+1]){
            return false;
        }
    }
    return true;
}
}
🧠 Why this is optimal

Time Complexity:
O(n) ✅
Single pass through the array
Stops early if disorder is found

Space Complexity:
O(1) ✅
No extra space used

Technique:
Linear traversal
Adjacent element comparison

Why not sorting?
Sorting would take O(n log n) ❌
We only need to check, not rearrange